  "primary_source_claim": "Hildebrand Theorem5.18/(5.32), printed166, gives unconditional integrated psi formula on x>=1, with full absolutely convergent zero series explained after(5.34), printed167. GM1312.4465v4 Eq1.3a printed2 and Lemma3.3 printed9 independently confirm formula/multiplicity/sign convention. Full primary locators and hashes in PERRON_SOURCE_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.json.",
  "proof_path_checks": [
    {
      "step": "actual population primitive",
      "finding": "psi1 is actual integral of Chebyshev.psi. Right continuity is proved from the floor definition. The right-derivative FTC/IBP accommodates actual psi jumps; no unproved continuity assumption on psi occurs."
    },
    {
      "step": "all-zero interchange",
      "finding": "Actual source summability at ordinaryx=2 gives summable coefficients. Complete open-strip bounds uniformly dominate every compact physical interval. Countable nonzero support is extracted from that summable coefficient family, not assumed for the entire subtype. Both endpoint sums and actual integrals are retained in the full operator interchange."
    },
    {
      "step": "zero packet normalization",
      "finding": "The actual derivative of t^(rho+1)/(rho(rho+1)) gives t^rho/rho, with multiplicity unchanged. Log substitution t=exp(L)*exp((s+u)delta) and the actual1/(2delta) yield precisely the original full complex zeroPacket, not a real-part surrogate or finite truncation."
    },
    {
      "step": "main/linear/additive terms",
      "finding": "Transport of t^2/2 gives actual mainAverage; transport of t*log(2pi) gives the exact constant. The arbitrary additive C is explicitly annihilated by constant_transport, so no unverified constant value is needed."
    },
    {
      "step": "trivial-zero sign/tail",
      "finding": "Complete primitive series is differentiated using a summable geometric majorant on actualx>1. Derivative is minus the original positive trivial correction. Original formula subtracts the primitive, so the final averaged identity adds actualtrivialAverage. No tail or endpoint is dropped."
    },
    {
      "step": "all-real domain/both shifts",
      "finding": "For every realL>=35 and actuals=-1 or1, physical lowerendpoint>1 and upper>=lower are proved; source used only there. Final identity is unconditional given the general source, without an added RH binder."
    },
    {
      "step": "actual final consumption",
      "finding": "box_explicit_formula_from_raw consumes integrated_source_normalized; final proof uses full summability, transported source, exact population/main/zero/linear/trivial identities and then real-part projection. It returns exactly the unchanged original canonical predicate."
    }
